course: dictionary
lesson: 7858
title: Rage: strong anger and great force
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rage is very strong anger that is hard to control. «Raj rage-quits FIFA when he's losing 5–0» means he leaves the game in a temper. He is too angry to keep playing.
explain: Rage can also be a verb. To rage means to be very angry and shout, as in «his aunt was raging» after the cousin ate a woodlouse. Storms, fires and seas can rage too, with great force.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Walking away also means walking away from your own rage» tells you that walking away is a way to stop being so angry. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Some phrases use rage in a different way. «All the rage» means very fashionable for a while, and it has nothing to do with anger. If anger does not fit the sentence, look for another meaning.
fact: Rage means very strong anger that is hard to control.
fact: To rage means to be very angry and shout, or to go on with great force, like a storm, fire or illness.
fact: «All the rage» means very fashionable for a while.
fact: Ways to calm rage include breathing slowly, counting to ten, walking away and talking about your feelings.
fact: «Rage-quitting» means leaving a game in a temper. It feels good for one second and can cost much more afterwards.
exercise: «Raj rage-quits FIFA when he's losing 5–0.» What does rage-quits mean here? | Asks a friend for help | *Leaves the game in a temper | Wins the game with a big score | Plays the game again to practise
exercise: «His aunt was raging.» What does raging mean? | *Very angry and shouting | Very tired and sleepy | Very happy and singing | Very hungry
exercise: Ollie says the new trainers are all the rage at school. What does all the rage mean? | Very angry at school | Very old and worn out | Stuck in a rage | *Very fashionable for a while
test: Which of these is a good way to calm rage? | Keep playing angrily | *Walk away and breathe slowly | Shout louder at everyone | Throw the controller across the room
test: «A storm began to rage across the sea.» What does rage mean here? | Stop suddenly | Be very fashionable | *Go on with great force | Feel very hungry
exam: «Walking away also means walking away from your own rage.» What is the best meaning of rage here? | *Very strong anger that is hard to control | A fashion trend for a while | A kind of weather | A type of game
